// Named workspaces. Included from config.kdl.
//
// Declaring them here makes them always exist, in this order, even when empty.
// That is the closest niri equivalent of sway's persistent-workspaces, and the
// waybar niri/workspaces module shows the name instead of the index for these.
//
// The existing Mod+1..Mod+9 binds still work: these take indices 1-3 in the
// order listed, so Mod+1 focuses "web", Mod+2 "term" and Mod+3 "misc". niri
// also keeps one empty unnamed workspace after the last one, which is normal.
//
// Names can also be changed at runtime with Mod+N, which does not persist.
workspace "web"
workspace "term"
workspace "misc"
